WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:04.518
You ran two days of drift
against an approved baseline,

3
00:00:04.518 --> 00:00:08.080
found three credentials
added outside the pipeline,

4
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:13.343
compared two A I inventory vintages,
packaged and chained both days, assembled

5
00:00:13.343 --> 00:00:18.200
a period for the ISSO, and saw an edited
file and a swapped package refused.

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.172
The evidence an ISSO keeps for
Gate 6 is each day's package,

7
00:00:22.172 --> 00:00:26.482
with its evidence manifest,
checksum file, summary and the run;

8
00:00:26.482 --> 00:00:30.201
the approved baseline's
hash; the vintage comparison;

9
00:00:30.201 --> 00:00:35.863
and the period's manifest and summary,
signed by the identity governance officer.

10
00:00:35.863 --> 00:00:38.937
Before you ship, work through
the chapter's checklist.

11
00:00:38.937 --> 00:00:43.888
Next is Module 11, the last:
deploy to test, then production.

12
00:00:43.888 --> 00:00:47.758
It runs every gate's code in one
safe order, with a preflight,

13
00:00:47.758 --> 00:00:52.730
a smoke test, an evidence record per
requirement and a rehearsed rollback.
